-Very well, thank you.

543
00:30:30,240 --> 00:30:32,440
-Je suis désolé. -C'est oublié.
-I'm sorry.
-It's forgotten.

544
00:30:32,560 --> 00:30:33,920
Je me suis emballé.
I got carried away.

545
00:30:35,800 --> 00:30:39,000
En tout cas, Gabor respecte votre décision.
In any case, Gabor respects your decision.

546
00:30:39,120 --> 00:30:43,040
C'était un grand coup pour lui, mais il ne vous en veut pas.
It was a big blow for him,
but he doesn't hold it against you.

547
00:30:43,160 --> 00:30:45,040
C'est un jeune homme brillant.
He's a bright young man.

548
00:30:45,120 --> 00:30:46,120
Comment va-t-il ?
How is he?

549
00:30:46,800 --> 00:30:50,400
À vrai dire... plutôt bien. Vraiment bien, même.
To tell the truth... pretty good.
Really good, actually.

550
00:30:50,480 --> 00:30:51,960
-Vraiment ? -Oui.
-Really?
-Yes.

551
00:30:52,600 --> 00:30:53,880
Je suis content de l'entendre.
I'm glad to hear it.

552
00:30:54,360 --> 00:30:56,400
Même si c'était un...
Even though it was a...

553
00:30:56,520 --> 00:30:58,360
Un choc, il s'en est vite remis.
A shock, he soon bounced back.

554
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:02,240
L'étincelle peut revenir si vite dans ce métier.
The spark can return so quickly
in this business.

555
00:31:02,360 --> 00:31:04,160
Oui, c'est vrai.
Yes, that's true.

556
00:31:05,960 --> 00:31:07,560
C'est encore confidentiel,
It's still confidential,

557
00:31:07,680 --> 00:31:10,640
mais vous faisiez partie du projet, alors je peux vous le dire.
but you were part of the project
so I can tell you.

558
00:31:11,280 --> 00:31:13,120
On prend Line Renaud.
We're going with Line Renaud.

559
00:31:15,120 --> 00:31:17,720
-Line... Line Renaud ? -Oui.
-Line... Line Renaud?
-Yes.

560
00:31:18,600 --> 00:31:21,960
C'est l'idée de Gabor. J'ai trouvé ça fou,
Gabor came up with the idea.
I thought it was crazy,

561
00:31:22,080 --> 00:31:25,000
vous et Line, vous n'avez rien en commun, mais...
you and Line couldn't be more different,
but...

562
00:31:25,560 --> 00:31:28,240
Françoise Fabian a décidé de ne pas faire le film.
Françoise Fabian
decided not to do the movie.

563
00:31:29,160 --> 00:31:31,200
Si près de la date de tournage !
That close to the starting date!

564
00:31:31,320 --> 00:31:32,800
Ce n'est vraiment pas bien.
That's not right at all.

565
00:31:34,520 --> 00:31:38,320
Apparemment, elle est fatiguée. Très fatiguée.
Apparently, she's tired. Very tired.

566
00:31:38,880 --> 00:31:40,520
Gabor est tellement enthousiaste.
Gabor is so keen.

567
00:31:40,640 --> 00:31:43,160
Il pense que c'est un contre-emploi formidable.
He thinks it's great casting against type.

568
00:31:43,280 --> 00:31:45,440
Il m'a convaincu, en tout cas.
He convinced me, anyway.

569
00:31:45,840 --> 00:31:47,200
C'est merveilleux.
That's wonderful.

570
00:31:47,920 --> 00:31:49,600
On la voit si rarement à l'écran.
You see her on-screen so rarely.

571
00:31:50,560 --> 00:31:52,280
C'était quoi, son dernier film ?
What was her last movie?

572
00:31:52,600 --> 00:31:53,800
Ah oui, Les Ch'tis.
Oh, yes, Les Ch'tis.

573
00:31:54,520 --> 00:31:55,520
Quel âge a-t-elle ?
How old is she?

574
00:31:55,920 --> 00:31:57,000
Je ne sais pas.
I don't know.

575
00:31:57,720 --> 00:31:59,760
Pour son dernier anniversaire,
For her last birthday,

576
00:31:59,880 --> 00:32:02,040
les bougies coûtaient plus cher que le gâteau !
the candles cost more than the cake!

577
00:32:04,960 --> 00:32:06,400
C'est une grande actrice.
She's a great actress.

578
00:32:06,520 --> 00:32:10,040
Oh oui, une grande actrice. Quel charme !
Oh, yes, a great actress. Such allure!

579
00:32:10,120 --> 00:32:13,720
Oui, ces yeux bleus, ce regard légendaire...
Yes, those blue eyes,
that legendary gaze...

580
00:32:13,800 --> 00:32:15,800
Quand elle apparaît dans un film,
When she appears in a movie,

581
00:32:15,920 --> 00:32:19,240
on se sent immédiatement... plus intelligent.
you immediately feel... smarter.

582
00:32:19,360 --> 00:32:22,320
Si elle jouait une nazie, vous la trouveriez séduisante.
If she played a Nazi,
you'd find her appealing.

583
00:32:22,400 --> 00:32:24,240
Elle est la femme française !
She's la femme française!

584
00:32:24,320 --> 00:32:26,551
Elle a une place dans le cœur de chaque Français.
She has a place
in every Frenchman's heart.

585
00:32:26,560 --> 00:32:31,240
Elle a une élégance très légèrement... inflexible.
She has an elegance
that's ever so slightly... unyielding.

586
00:32:31,760 --> 00:32:33,840
Elle peut faire peur.
She can be scary.

587
00:32:33,920 --> 00:32:35,920
C'est l'éternelle amie des femmes.
She's the eternal female friend.

588
00:32:38,120 --> 00:32:41,440
-Je pense toujours que le rôle était fait pour vous. -Vraiment ?
-I still think the role was made for you.
-Really?

589
00:32:44,080 --> 00:32:45,920
J'ai retourné Françoise Fabian.
I've turned Françoise Fabian.

590
00:32:46,000 --> 00:32:47,400
-Non. -Si !
-No.
-Yeah!

591
00:32:47,520 --> 00:32:49,560
Elle revient pour faire le film.
She's coming back to do the movie.

592
00:32:49,680 --> 00:32:51,920
-Comment vous avez fait ? -J'ai fait un Mathias.
-How did you do it?
-I did a Mathias.

593
00:32:52,000 --> 00:32:55,280
Je lui ai dit que Gabor voulait Line Renaud.
I told her that Gabor wanted Line Renaud.

594
00:32:55,360 --> 00:32:57,480
Je l'ai manipulée avec des mensonges.
I manipulated her with lies.

595
00:32:58,040 --> 00:33:01,000
-Je déteste faire ça. -Je sais, mais ça fait tellement de bien !
-I hate doing that.
-I know, but it feels so good!

596
00:33:01,320 --> 00:33:04,520
Trouver le point G de l'envie de vivre d'une actrice !
Finding the G-spot
of an actress's lust for life!

597
00:33:05,560 --> 00:33:07,280
Le pouvoir de la rivalité.
The power of rivalry.

598
00:33:07,920 --> 00:33:09,760
C'est un beau métier, non ?
This is a great business, huh?

599
00:33:10,120 --> 00:33:11,040
Tout va bien.
All is well.

600
00:33:11,160 --> 00:33:13,680
Le film est sauvé, Gabor va être aux anges.
The movie's saved, Gabor will be ecstatic.

601
00:33:17,680 --> 00:33:19,880
-Quand j'y pense... -Quoi ?
-When I think about it...
-What?

602
00:33:20,280 --> 00:33:22,920
Line Renaud dans un film de Gabor Rajevski.
Line Renaud in a Gabor Rajevski movie.

603
00:33:23,040 --> 00:33:24,200
C'est absurde !
It's absurd!

604
00:33:25,560 --> 00:33:26,440
Oui ?
Yes?

605
00:33:26,520 --> 00:33:27,920
Il me veut !
He wants me!

606
00:33:28,520 --> 00:33:30,880
Je viens de passer deux heures avec Gabor.
I just spent two hours with Gabor.

607
00:33:31,520 --> 00:33:35,240
On est amoureux ! On tourne dans trois semaines, les enfants !
We're in love! We start shooting
in three weeks, children!

608
00:33:35,360 --> 00:33:36,720
Merci, Gabi.
Thank you, Gabi.

609
00:33:38,320 --> 00:33:41,200
Mon petit miracle ! Champagne !
My little miracle! Champagne!

610
00:33:41,960 --> 00:33:43,360
On fait quelle impression ?
What do we look like?

611
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:45,680
Celle de gens de goût, Andréa.
Like discerning people, Andréa.

612
00:33:45,795 --> 00:33:47,920
Des gens qui comprennent le cinéma de Gabor,
People who understand Gabor's cinema,

613
00:33:48,040 --> 00:33:51,440
et dont l'intuition peut sauver les situations les plus désespérées.
and whose intuition can save
the most desperate situations.

614
00:33:51,560 --> 00:33:53,760
Personne ne t'a demandé d'intervenir.
No one asked you to interfere.

615
00:33:53,880 --> 00:33:55,760
Non, tu paniquais.
No, you were freaking out.

616
00:33:55,880 --> 00:33:58,560
Mais j'avais quand même la situation en main !
But I was still in control
of the situation!

617
00:33:58,680 --> 00:33:59,630
Je voulais t'aider.
I wanted to help.

618
00:33:59,760 --> 00:34:02,120
Tu faisais le beau devant ton nouveau client !
You were showing off to your new client!

619
00:34:02,800 --> 00:34:05,880
Ce rôle n'a été écrit que pour Françoise Fabian !
That part wasn't written for anyone
but Françoise Fabian!

620
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:08,760
Alors dis à Line Renaud de dégager !
So tell Line Renaud to get out of the way!

621
00:34:08,840 --> 00:34:12,280
Vas donc dire à Françoise Fabian que le rôle est pris !
You go tell Françoise Fabian
that the part's already taken!

622
00:34:12,400 --> 00:34:14,840
Gabriel, je ne plaisante pas ! Fais ce que je dis !
Gabriel, I'm not playing! Do as I say!

623
00:34:14,960 --> 00:34:16,520
Ne me donne pas d'ordres !
Do not order me around!

624
00:34:16,630 --> 00:34:19,320
Tu ne fais que tout gâcher !
All you do is screw things up!

625
00:34:19,440 --> 00:34:21,880
Tu ne fais qu'insulter tes clients !
All you do is insult your clients!

626
00:34:22,000 --> 00:34:24,160
Tu n'as besoin de personne, Andréa !
You don't need anyone, Andréa!

627
00:34:24,280 --> 00:34:27,160
En tout cas pas de toi et de tes idées stupides !
I certainly don't need you
and your stupid ideas!

628
00:34:31,360 --> 00:34:33,880
Et quand tu auras 40 ans et voudras un enfant,
And when you're 40 and want a kid,

629
00:34:33,960 --> 00:34:35,760
trouve quelqu'un d'autre pour ça aussi !
find someone else for that, too!

630
00:34:37,680 --> 00:34:38,760
Exactement !
Exactly!

631
00:34:50,720 --> 00:34:54,680
Donc je garderai bien 17 % des parts ?
So, I will still own 17 percent
of the shares?

632
00:34:54,800 --> 00:34:57,120
Oui. Nous pensions que...
Yes. We thought that...

633
00:34:57,720 --> 00:35:00,600
vous apprécieriez ces revenus en souvenir de Samuel.
you'd appreciate the income
in memory of Samuel.

634
00:35:01,440 --> 00:35:04,240
Vous n'avez rien à faire, vous toucherez simplement les bénéfices.
There's nothing to do,
you'll just get the profits.

635
00:35:05,040 --> 00:35:07,120
Comme c'est gentil de penser à ma retraite.
How nice of you to think of my pension.

636
00:35:07,404 --> 00:35:10,080
À moins que la vraie raison soit que vous quatre
Unless the real reason
is that the four of you

637
00:35:10,160 --> 00:35:12,640
n'ayez pas pu réunir assez pour racheter toutes les parts.
couldn't raise enough
to buy all the shares.

638
00:35:14,560 --> 00:35:17,720
Nous avons fait un énorme effort pour vous soumettre cette offre, Hélène.
We've made a huge effort
to make you this offer, Hélène.

639
00:35:17,840 --> 00:35:21,640
Gabriel a hypothéqué son appartement, Andréa a pris un crédit sur 20 ans,
Gabriel's mortgaged his apartment,
Andréa's taken a 20-year loan,

640
00:35:21,720 --> 00:35:23,560
l'assurance-vie d'Arlette...
Arlette's life insurance...

641
00:35:23,680 --> 00:35:27,000
Et vous devenez actionnaire majoritaire et patron d'ASK.
And you become the majority shareholder
and boss of ASK.

642
00:35:29,440 --> 00:35:31,040
En augmentant nos bénéfices,
By increasing our profits,

643
00:35:31,120 --> 00:35:35,360
nous pourrons vous racheter entièrement d'ici un an environ.
we'll be able to buy you out completely
in about a year.

644
00:35:42,920 --> 00:35:46,120
Avez-vous déjà trompé votre femme, Mathias ?
Have you ever cheated
on your wife, Mathias ?

645
00:35:47,360 --> 00:35:50,080
Pardonnez-moi, mais je ne suis pas du genre à me confier.
Sorry, but I'm not the confiding sort.

646
00:35:51,280 --> 00:35:54,200
Samuel m'a beaucoup trompée, surtout avec des actrices.
Samuel cheated on me a lot,
usually with actresses.

647
00:35:54,320 --> 00:35:57,200
-Mais j'imagine que vous le saviez. -Pas vraiment, non.
-But I imagine you knew that.
-Not really, no.

648
00:35:58,600 --> 00:36:00,960
On pourrait croire qu'en vieillissant,
You'd think that as you grow older,

649
00:36:01,080 --> 00:36:04,440
on finit par accepter, par s'y faire...
you'd come to terms with it, accept it...

650
00:36:04,760 --> 00:36:05,960
Ce ne fut pas mon cas.
I didn't.

651
00:36:07,560 --> 00:36:09,160
Je vais vous dire quelque chose.
I'll tell you something.

652
00:36:10,600 --> 00:36:12,960
Je déteste les actrices.
I hate actresses.

653
00:36:14,880 --> 00:36:16,160
Alors, vous comprenez...
So, you see...

654
00:36:16,720 --> 00:36:21,120
l'idée de toucher un pourcentage sur leurs cachets me dégoûte.
the thought of getting a percentage
from their performances disgusts me.

655
00:36:24,560 --> 00:36:28,360
Désolée, Mathias, mais je dois examiner les autres offres qu'on m'a faites.
Sorry, Mathias, but I'll have to look
at the other offers I've had.

656
00:36:28,480 --> 00:36:30,720
-L'addition, s'il vous plaît. -D'autres offres ?
-The check, please.
-Other offers?

657
00:36:30,840 --> 00:36:31,800
Oh, oui.
Oh, yes.

658
00:36:32,400 --> 00:36:35,960
Les gens sont toujours trop prompts à sauter sur les cadavres.
People are only too quick
to come jumping over dead bodies.

659
00:36:54,360 --> 00:36:55,720
Au revoir, Sofia.
See you, Sofia.

660
00:36:56,000 --> 00:36:56,920
Au revoir.
See you.

661
00:37:55,640 --> 00:37:56,480
Bonsoir.
Hi.

662
00:37:57,000 --> 00:38:00,240
Il est vraiment tard. Andréa est déjà partie.
It's really late. Andréa's already gone.

663
00:38:00,760 --> 00:38:02,640
-Bonsoir. -Oui, désolé.
-Good evening.
-Yes, sorry.

664
00:38:03,800 --> 00:38:05,200
Qu'est-ce que je peux faire pour vous ?
What can I do for you?

665
00:38:06,240 --> 00:38:08,360
Andréa m'a laissé un scénario ici.
Andréa left a script here for me.

666
00:38:08,480 --> 00:38:10,680
Non, elle n'a rien laissé.
No, she didn't.

667
00:38:12,880 --> 00:38:14,000
Voyez par vous-même !
See for yourself!

668
00:38:18,840 --> 00:38:19,840
Merci, Camille.
Thanks, Camille.

669
00:38:22,360 --> 00:38:23,200
Imaginez...
Imagine...

670
00:38:23,280 --> 00:38:25,480
qu'il y a une ligne invisible entre nous.
there's an invisible line between us.

671
00:38:25,880 --> 00:38:28,800
Si je vous filme comme ça au début...
If I film you like this at the start...

672
00:38:28,920 --> 00:38:31,800
C'est un truc bizarre que font les réalisateurs,
That's something weird that directors do,

673
00:38:31,920 --> 00:38:34,160
pour visualiser le plan.
to imagine the shot.

674
00:38:35,960 --> 00:38:37,320
Même pas beau.
It doesn't even look good.

675
00:38:38,160 --> 00:38:40,480
Il y a encore des gens qui veulent essayer.
There are still people who want to try.

676
00:38:40,640 --> 00:38:44,160
Ma mère donne de petits cours de coiffure...
My mom does these little classes
in hair styling...

677
00:38:44,280 --> 00:38:48,080
Sur vous, par exemple, je vois que ça demande du travail.
On you, for example,
I can see that takes work.

678
00:38:48,240 --> 00:38:51,400
-C'est quelle star ? -Personne !
-Which star is that?
-No one!

679
00:38:53,400 --> 00:38:54,880
Quand vous regardez des films...
When you watch movies...

680
00:38:56,160 --> 00:38:57,320
des scènes d'amour...
love scenes...

681
00:38:58,120 --> 00:38:59,400
Ils le font vraiment.
They really do it.

682
00:38:59,960 --> 00:39:01,800
-Non. -Si, ils le font pour de vrai.
-No.
-Yes, they do it for real.

683
00:39:02,320 --> 00:39:03,520
Ils s'embrassent vraiment.
They really kiss.

684
00:39:12,920 --> 00:39:14,680
Ils font ça comme ça ?
They do it like that?

685
00:39:20,360 --> 00:39:21,280
Plus ou moins.
More or less.

686
00:39:34,040 --> 00:39:36,960
Comment Gabor peut-il hésiter entre les deux ?
How could Gabor be unsure
about which one to choose?

687
00:39:38,040 --> 00:39:40,280
Il rêvait de Françoise pour ce rôle.
He dreamt of Françoise for that part.

688
00:39:41,240 --> 00:39:44,080
Bon, Line a vraiment quelque chose, mais...
Okay, Line really has something, but...

689
00:39:45,920 --> 00:39:47,040
Honnêtement, non.
To be honest, no.

690
00:39:51,560 --> 00:39:54,640
Qu'est-ce que je vais dire à Françoise s'il ne la veut plus ?
What will I tell Françoise
if he doesn't want her now?

691
00:39:56,960 --> 00:39:58,200
C'est pas possible !
I don't believe this!

692
00:39:58,440 --> 00:39:59,960
Je n'arrive pas à me concentrer !
I can't concentrate!

693
00:40:00,080 --> 00:40:01,280
Je suis désolé.
I'm sorry.

694
00:40:09,560 --> 00:40:10,480
Désolée.
Sorry.

695
00:40:10,560 --> 00:40:12,120
WHITE ZOMBIE
WHITE ZOMBIE

696
00:40:12,200 --> 00:40:15,866
SOUS SON EMPRISE DE ZOMBIE, IL LUI FAISAIT ACCOMPLIR TOUS SES DÉSIRS
WITH THIS ZOMBIE GRIP
HE MADE HER PERFORM HIS EVERY DESIRE

697
00:40:48,240 --> 00:40:49,120
Quoi de neuf ?
What's up?

698
00:40:50,080 --> 00:40:52,200
Les funérailles de Samuel Kerr. Je vais être en retard.
Samuel Kerr's funeral. I'll be late.

699
00:40:52,960 --> 00:40:54,320
Où sont mes affaires ?
Where are my things?

700
00:40:54,440 --> 00:40:56,240
Je t'emmène sur mon scooter.
I'll take you on my scooter.

701
00:40:57,000 --> 00:40:57,880
Vraiment ?
Really?

702
00:40:58,720 --> 00:41:00,782
Trop sympa ! Corrige-moi si je me trompe.
So fucking sweet! Correct me if I'm wrong.

703
00:41:13,280 --> 00:41:16,480
Françoise Fabian et Line Renaud veulent le même rôle,
Françoise Fabian and Line Renaud
want the same part,

704
00:41:16,600 --> 00:41:19,280
et celle qui ne l'obtient pas nous détestera,
and whichever one doesn't get it
will hate us,

705
00:41:19,400 --> 00:41:21,960
quittera l'agence et détruira notre réputation ?
leave the agency
and destroy our reputation?

706
00:41:22,080 --> 00:41:23,080
C'est bien ça ?
Is that right?

707
00:41:23,600 --> 00:41:25,320
Comment on s'est mis dans une telle merde ?
How did we get in such shit?

708
00:41:25,440 --> 00:41:26,600
Demande à Gabriel.
Ask Gabriel.

709
00:41:27,160 --> 00:41:28,160
Demande à Andréa.
Ask Andréa.

710
00:41:30,560 --> 00:41:32,320
On ne peut pas conclure une trêve ?
Can't we call a truce?

711
00:41:33,520 --> 00:41:35,520
On enterre Samuel, tu te souviens ?
We're burying Samuel, remember?

712
00:42:38,160 --> 00:42:39,480
Merci.
Thank you.

713
00:42:46,200 --> 00:42:47,360
Bonsoir.
Good evening.

714
00:42:48,280 --> 00:42:51,440
Au nom d'ASK, je vous remercie d'être venus.
On behalf of ASK,
I'd like to thank you for coming.

715
00:42:52,000 --> 00:42:55,920
Je laisse la parole à une grande amie de Samuel,
I'll hand over
to a great friend of Samuel,

716
00:42:56,000 --> 00:42:57,560
Mme Françoise Fabian.
Mrs. Françoise Fabian.

717
00:43:02,520 --> 00:43:03,520
Bonsoir.
Good evening.

718
00:43:06,080 --> 00:43:09,040
Il y a quelques semaines, je dînais avec Samuel.
A few weeks ago,
I was having dinner with Samuel.

719
00:43:11,600 --> 00:43:15,400
Il a dit quelque chose de merveilleux qui résonne encore en moi aujourd'hui :
He said something wonderful
which still resonates with me today:

720
00:43:16,040 --> 00:43:18,240
« Quelle chance vous avez, vous les acteurs...
"How lucky you actors are...

721
00:43:19,040 --> 00:43:21,200
avoir un métier qui consiste à « jouer ».
to have a job
which is all about 'playing.'

722
00:43:22,200 --> 00:43:24,720
C'est pour ça que vous restez des enfants : vous jouez des rôles.
That's why you remain children:
you play parts.

723
00:43:25,360 --> 00:43:29,480
Vous jouez pour ne pas grandir, vous jouez pour ne pas mourir."
You play so as not to grow up,
you play so as not to die."

724
00:43:31,000 --> 00:43:35,200
Samuel, nous essayons de rester de grands enfants pleins de passion.
Samuel, we try to remain
big children full of passion.

725
00:43:35,800 --> 00:43:39,800
Mais en ce jour de tristesse, nous n'avons pas le cœur à jouer.
But on this sad day,
we're not in the mood for playing.

726
00:43:42,560 --> 00:43:44,760
Tu nous manques terriblement.
We miss you terribly.

727
00:43:47,560 --> 00:43:48,520
Merci.
Thank you.

728
00:43:51,080 --> 00:43:53,720
Il n'aurait pas voulu qu'on pleure. N'est-ce pas ?
He wouldn't have wanted us to cry.
Would you?

729
00:43:54,280 --> 00:43:55,840
Tu aurais voulu qu'on rie !
You'd have wanted us to laugh!

730
00:43:55,920 --> 00:43:59,520
Samou était plein de joie, libre,
Samou was full of joy, free,

731
00:43:59,600 --> 00:44:01,200
un fou furieux !
a mad dog!

732
00:44:01,520 --> 00:44:04,280
Comme on faisait la fête, dans le temps.
How we used to party, back in the day.

733
00:44:05,080 --> 00:44:09,680
On s'est tellement amusés une fois que je suis montée sur scène en pouffant
We had so much fun one time,
that I went on stage still giggling

734
00:44:09,760 --> 00:44:12,440
et je n'arrivais même pas à commencer ma chanson !
and couldn't even start my song!

735
00:44:15,240 --> 00:44:17,120
Tu nous manques, Samou.
We miss you, Samou.

736
00:44:18,080 --> 00:44:20,080
Mais je te promets une chose.
But I promise you one thing.

737
00:44:20,160 --> 00:44:22,560
Nous continuerons à rire...
We shall continue to laugh...

738
00:44:23,480 --> 00:44:27,640
même si ton absence nous donne envie de pleurer ce soir.
however much your absence
makes us want to cry tonight.

739
00:44:27,760 --> 00:44:28,840
Merci, Samou.
Thank you, Samou.

740
00:44:31,760 --> 00:44:33,280
Oui, il faut se battre contre le chagrin.
Yes, we must fight sorrow.

741
00:44:34,920 --> 00:44:37,480
Samuel aimait vraiment rire...
Samuel really enjoyed laughter...

742
00:44:38,680 --> 00:44:41,320
mais c'était aussi un homme de grande profondeur.
but he was also a man of great depth.

743
00:44:42,960 --> 00:44:46,320
La lumière de ton intelligence s'est éteinte, Samuel...
The light of your intelligence
has gone out, Samuel...

744
00:44:47,320 --> 00:44:49,360
nous laissant tous dans le noir.
leaving us all in the dark.

745
00:44:51,360 --> 00:44:52,240
Merci.
Thank you.

746
00:44:53,920 --> 00:44:56,080
Tu aimais une belle chanson...
You loved a good song...

747
00:44:56,600 --> 00:44:58,440
celle-là surtout.
especially this one.

748
00:44:58,520 --> 00:45:01,560
Tu disais que c'était « notre chanson ».
You used to say this was "our song."

749
00:45:44,120 --> 00:45:46,000
Oui, dis-nous, Samou.
Yes, tell us, Samou.

750
00:46:23,840 --> 00:46:25,240
Pourquoi ne pas prendre les deux ?
Why not take them both?

751
00:46:26,320 --> 00:46:28,560
Bonnie et Clyde à 80 ans, c'est iconoclaste,
Bonnie and Clyde at 80 is iconoclastic,

752
00:46:28,680 --> 00:46:30,280
mais avec deux femmes,
but with two women,

753
00:46:30,360 --> 00:46:32,480
ça devient moderne, féministe...
it becomes modern, feminist...

754
00:46:32,560 --> 00:46:34,880
La Vie d'Adèle rencontre Tarantino !
Blue is the Warmest Color meets Tarantino!

755
00:46:35,000 --> 00:46:37,720
-Vous voulez dire un vrai couple de femmes. -Oui.
-You mean a real female couple.
-Yes.

756
00:46:37,800 --> 00:46:39,440
Des lesbiennes, mais âgées.
Lesbians, but elderly.

757
00:46:39,960 --> 00:46:43,240
Line Renaud, Françoise Fabian. On vient de les voir.
Line Renaud, Françoise Fabian.
We just saw them.

758
00:46:43,360 --> 00:46:45,760
Chacune est une star, mais dans son propre genre.
Each one is a star, but in her own genre.

759
00:46:45,840 --> 00:46:47,160
Mais ensemble...
But together...

760
00:46:47,240 --> 00:46:49,280
Vous avez vu comment elles ont enflammé ça ?
Did you see how they lit it up?

761
00:46:50,280 --> 00:46:52,920
Elles sont nées braqueurs !
They're born hold-up artists!

762
00:46:53,720 --> 00:46:56,440
Si on ne gagne pas la Palme d'Or à Cannes...
If we don't win
the Palme d'Or at Cannes...

763
00:46:57,080 --> 00:46:58,120
je raccroche !
I'll quit!

764
00:46:58,880 --> 00:47:00,160
C'est pas mal.
That's not bad.

765
00:47:00,240 --> 00:47:02,600
C'est totalement inattendu, c'est...
It's totally unexpected, it's...

766
00:47:02,720 --> 00:47:04,920
radicalement irrévérencieux.
radically irreverent.

767
00:47:05,000 --> 00:47:07,080
Tout le monde en parlera.
Everyone will be talking about it.

768
00:47:07,200 --> 00:47:09,360
Et vous avez deux stars au casting !
And you get two stars cast!

769
00:47:09,440 --> 00:47:11,800
-On vous fait un bon prix. -Bien sûr.
-We'll give you a good price.
-Of course.

770
00:47:14,480 --> 00:47:15,320
Outjet !
Outjet!

771
00:47:17,320 --> 00:47:18,360
Oui, outjet.
Yes, outjet.

772
00:47:21,400 --> 00:47:23,520
Eh bien... Outjet !
Well, then... Outjet!

773
00:47:25,080 --> 00:47:25,920
Outjet !
Outjet!

774
00:47:27,880 --> 00:47:30,280
-Vous en voulez ? -Non, merci.
-Would you care for some?
-No, thanks.

775
00:47:31,040 --> 00:47:33,680
Tu as couru ? Dans le cimetière ?
You had to run? In the cemetery?

776
00:47:33,800 --> 00:47:35,520
Oui, j'ai couru dans le cimetière.
Yes, I ran in the cemetery.

777
00:47:35,640 --> 00:47:38,600
-Tout le monde était autour de la tombe et toi... -Hippolyte !
-Everyone was around the grave and you...
-Hippolyte!

778
00:47:41,760 --> 00:47:43,840
-Voici Catherine, ma mère. -Bonjour.
-This is Catherine, my mom.
-Hello.

779
00:47:44,800 --> 00:47:47,560
Voici Camille, la nouvelle assistante d'Andréa Martel.
This is Camille,
Andréa Martel's new assistant.

780
00:47:48,440 --> 00:47:50,480
Pauvre vous !
Poor you!

781
00:47:50,560 --> 00:47:52,320
-Tu connaissais bien Samuel ? -Oui.
-You knew Samuel well?
-Yes.

782
00:47:52,880 --> 00:47:55,466
Mon mari a travaillé avec lui pendant plus de 15 ans.
My husband worked with him
for over 15 years.

783
00:47:55,520 --> 00:47:57,680
Quand on parle du loup. Mathias !
Speak of the devil. Mathias!

784
00:48:02,600 --> 00:48:04,360
Toute la famille est là maintenant.
The whole family's here now.

785
00:48:04,920 --> 00:48:06,675
Les présentations ne sont pas nécessaires.
No introductions necessary.

786
00:48:07,480 --> 00:48:09,400
Camille est l'assistante d'Andréa.
Camille is Andréa's assistant.

787
00:48:10,320 --> 00:48:11,840
Oui, Hippolyte me l'a dit.
Yes, Hippolyte told me.

788
00:48:12,880 --> 00:48:15,560
Je ne savais pas que votre fils était acteur.
I didn't know your son was an actor.

789
00:48:16,840 --> 00:48:18,640
Tu aurais pu me le dire !
You could have told me!

790
00:48:19,200 --> 00:48:20,360
Qu'est-ce que ça change ?
What does it change?

791
00:48:24,680 --> 00:48:25,760
J'ai soif.
I'm thirsty.

792
00:48:26,720 --> 00:48:27,920
On va prendre un verre ?
Shall we get a drink?

793
00:48:34,520 --> 00:48:35,800
J'ai vraiment envie de toi !
I really want you!

794
00:48:35,880 --> 00:48:38,200
Non, quelqu'un pourrait entrer.
No, someone might come in.

795
00:48:38,760 --> 00:48:40,360
Personne ne va entrer.
No one will come in.

796
00:48:40,920 --> 00:48:42,360
Attends, juste...
Hang on, just...

797
00:48:42,480 --> 00:48:45,520
Je me souviens pas vraiment. On a fait quoi hier soir ?
I don't really remember.
What did we do last night?

798
00:48:45,640 --> 00:48:48,240
-Ça t'excite, hein ? -Hippolyte, vraiment !
-That gets you hot, huh?
-Really, Hippolyte!

799
00:48:49,240 --> 00:48:50,160
Vraiment ?
Really?

800
00:48:51,120 --> 00:48:52,960
Tu ne te souviens de rien ?
You don't remember anything?

801
00:48:53,040 --> 00:48:54,280
On a... ?
Did we...?

802
00:48:56,040 --> 00:48:57,680
On a quoi ? Baisé ?
Did we what? Screw?

803
00:48:57,760 --> 00:48:58,640
Ouais.
Yeah.

804
00:48:59,760 --> 00:49:02,160
T'es pas capable de le dire quand t'es sobre ?
Can't you say the word when you're sober?

805
00:49:02,240 --> 00:49:03,400
Dis-moi !
Tell me!

806
00:49:04,240 --> 00:49:07,320
On est rentrés chez moi, on s'est embrassés,
We went back to my place, we made out,

807
00:49:07,400 --> 00:49:08,760
je t'ai portée jusqu'à mon lit,
I carried you to my bed,

808
00:49:08,880 --> 00:49:11,440
je t'ai bordée et... rien.
I tucked you in and... nothing.

809
00:49:11,560 --> 00:49:14,320
-Tu t'es endormie en deux secondes. -Vraiment ?
-You fell asleep in two seconds.
-Really?

810
00:49:15,040 --> 00:49:16,040
Oui, vraiment.
Yes, really.

811
00:49:16,840 --> 00:49:17,960
Merci !
Thank you!

812
00:49:24,840 --> 00:49:28,080
Un film de Tavernier sur la guerre d'Algérie. Super !
A Tavernier movie about the Algerian War.
Great!

813
00:49:28,160 --> 00:49:31,280
Il n'y a pas de rôle pour toi. Que quelques personnages kabyles.
There's no part for you.
Only a few Kabyle characters.

814
00:49:31,400 --> 00:49:33,400
Quoi, j'ai pas l'air kabyle ?
What, don't I look like a Kabyle?

815
00:49:34,600 --> 00:49:37,880
Et le film de Gallienne ? Je peux lire le scénario ?
What about Gallienne's movie?
Can I read the script?

816
00:49:38,000 --> 00:49:39,120
Qu'est-ce qui se passe ?
What's happening?

817
00:49:39,240 --> 00:49:41,720
Dis-moi au moins de quoi ça parle.
At least tell me what it's about.

818
00:49:46,760 --> 00:49:48,440
Désolée pour hier.
Sorry about yesterday.

819
00:49:49,480 --> 00:49:51,280
Line Renaud, c'était une idée de génie.
Line Renaud was a genius idea.

820
00:49:52,920 --> 00:49:54,080
Moi aussi, je suis désolée.
I'm sorry, too.

821
00:49:55,360 --> 00:49:58,360
Je ne t'abandonnerai pas quand tu veux un enfant à 40 ans.
I won't abandon you
when you want a baby at 40.

822
00:50:00,440 --> 00:50:01,920
Je t'emmènerai en Hollande.
I'll take you to Holland.

823
00:50:02,040 --> 00:50:03,120
Salaud !
Bastard!

824
00:50:04,920 --> 00:50:08,360
Sans toi, je crois que j'arrêterais ce métier.
If it wasn't for you,
I think I might quit this business.

825
00:50:08,760 --> 00:50:10,200
Oui, Sue Ellen !
Yes, Sue Ellen!

826
00:50:18,000 --> 00:50:20,200
À quoi tu joues avec mon fils ?
What are you playing at with my son?

827
00:50:20,280 --> 00:50:21,960
Je ne savais pas que c'était ton fils.
I didn't know he was your son.

828
00:50:22,080 --> 00:50:23,200
Il ne me l'a pas dit.
He didn't tell me.

829
00:50:23,320 --> 00:50:24,680
-Tu lui as fait du rentre-dedans ? -Non !
-Did you hit on him?
-No!

830
00:50:24,800 --> 00:50:25,960
-Ah bon ? -Non !
-Yeah?
-No!

831
00:50:26,040 --> 00:50:29,680
-Tu es complètement irresponsable ! -C'est un comble, venant de toi !
-You're being totally reckless!
-That's rich, coming from you!

832
00:50:29,800 --> 00:50:32,520
C'est toi qui mens à tout le monde !
You're the one who lies to everybody!

833
00:50:32,640 --> 00:50:34,320
Tu es une lâche !
You're a coward!

834
00:50:34,400 --> 00:50:37,057
-Ta gueule ! -Tu n'as jamais assumé ce qu'on était !
-Shut up!
-You never took responsibility for us!

835
00:50:38,280 --> 00:50:39,920
Reste loin de ma famille.
Keep away from my family.

836
00:50:40,480 --> 00:50:41,840
Je fais partie de ta famille, moi aussi !
I'm your family, too!

837
00:51:03,760 --> 00:51:05,200
T'as du feu, Noémie ?
Do you have a light, Noémie?

838
00:51:05,320 --> 00:51:06,480
Non, je ne fume pas.
No, I don't smoke.

839
00:51:21,760 --> 00:51:22,840
Merci.
Thanks.

840
00:51:28,120 --> 00:51:29,240
C'est rien.
Don't sweat it.

841
00:51:32,640 --> 00:51:35,240
Les chagrins, les hommes...
Sorrows, men...

842
00:51:36,040 --> 00:51:37,840
tout part en fumée.
they all go up in smoke.
